{% comment %}
  Self-contained purchase widget: image-swatch variant picker, quantity, a
  bundle picker (one card per selling plan -- clicking a card both picks that
  plan and shows its price), and its own add-to-cart button. There is no
  one-time-purchase option; every add-to-cart from this widget is a
  subscription on whichever plan's card is selected.

  If the product has no selling plan group at all, this block renders nothing
  at all -- no fallback buy box of its own. The theme's own default variant
  picker / add-to-cart button (already on the page) is what shows for those
  products; this widget only takes over the purchase UI when there's actually
  something to subscribe to.

  Every label/heading/button-copy string below comes from block.settings (set
  per-instance in the theme editor) rather than being hardcoded, so merchants
  can reword this for products where e.g. the first option isn't a "flavor".
  Only genuinely product-derived values (price, discount %, delivery cadence,
  which plan is the best deal) are computed live from Shopify's own product/
  selling-plan data in subscription-widget.js -- never hardcoded.

  Because this renders its own buy button, merchants should remove or hide the
  theme's default variant picker / buy buttons block specifically on products
  that DO have a subscription, to avoid two purchase forms on the same page --
  for products with no subscription, both can coexist since this block stays
  empty for them.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign selling_plan_group = product.selling_plan_groups.first -%}
{%- assign has_subscription = false -%}
{%- if selling_plan_group and selling_plan_group.selling_plans.size > 0 -%}
  {%- assign has_subscription = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if has_subscription -%}
  {%- assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}

  <div
    class="subscription-widget"
    style="--subscription-widget-accent: {{ block.settings.accent_color }}; --subscription-widget-swatch-selected: {{ block.settings.swatch_selected_color }};"
    data-subscription-widget
    data-has-subscription="true"
    data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <script type="application/json" data-subscription-widget-product>
      {{ product | json }}
    </script>
    <script type="application/json" data-subscription-widget-settings>
      {
        "subscribeButtonLabel": {{ block.settings.subscribe_button_label | json }},
        "bestValueBadgeText": {{ block.settings.best_value_badge_text | json }},
        "showBestValueBadge": {{ block.settings.show_best_value_badge | json }},
        "moneyFormat": {{ shop.money_format | json }}
      }
    </script>

    {%- comment -%}
      Sticky add-to-cart bar: hidden by default, shown by subscription-widget.js
      once the main order summary's own submit button scrolls out of view. Its
      plan selector and price mirror whichever plan/variant is selected in the
      main widget above -- and picking a plan here updates that same state, so
      both stay in sync in either direction. Content is filled in/kept in sync
      entirely by render() in subscription-widget.js; the option buttons below
      are just empty shells keyed by plan id.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar" data-sticky-bar hidden>
      <span class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-media">
        <img data-sticky-image alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56" hidden>
      </span>
      <span class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-title" data-sticky-title>{{ product.title }}</span>

      <div class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan" data-sticky-plan>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan-trigger"
          data-sticky-plan-trigger
          aria-haspopup="listbox"
          aria-expanded="false"
        >
          <span class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan-text">
            <span class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan-label" data-sticky-plan-label></span>
            <span class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan-sub" data-sticky-plan-sub></span>
          </span>
          <svg width="12" height="8" viewBox="0 0 12 8" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M1 1.5L6 6.5L11 1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <ul class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan-list" data-sticky-plan-list role="listbox" hidden>
          {%- for plan in selling_plan_group.selling_plans -%}
            <li role="presentation">
              <button
                type="button"
                class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan-option"
                data-sticky-plan-option
                data-plan-id="{{ plan.id }}"
                role="option"
              >
                <span class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan-option-label" data-option-label></span>
                <span class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-plan-option-sub" data-option-sub></span>
              </button>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <button type="button" class="subscription-widget__sticky-bar-submit" data-sticky-add-to-cart>
        <span data-sticky-submit-label></span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="subscription-widget__section">
      {%- if block.settings.plan_step_label != blank -%}
        <p class="subscription-widget__step-label">{{ block.settings.plan_step_label }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <p class="subscription-widget__plan-heading">{{ block.settings.plan_section_label }}</p>

      {%- comment -%}
        Bundle images come straight from the theme editor -- a merchant picks
        them per plan SLOT (1st/2nd/3rd plan in the group), the same way any
        other theme image setting works. No upload/API plumbing needed: this
        sidesteps the fact that Liquid can't query this app's own database at
        render time, which is what would otherwise be needed to show an image
        uploaded through the app's own admin.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="subscription-widget__bundle-grid">
        {%- for plan in selling_plan_group.selling_plans -%}
          {%- case forloop.index -%}
            {%- when 1 -%}{%- assign bundle_image = block.settings.bundle_image_1 -%}
            {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign bundle_image = block.settings.bundle_image_2 -%}
            {%- when 3 -%}{%- assign bundle_image = block.settings.bundle_image_3 -%}
            {%- else -%}{%- assign bundle_image = nil -%}
          {%- endcase -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Liquid's selling_plan object has no billing_policy/interval_count
            field (unlike the Admin/Storefront GraphQL APIs) -- the day count
            only exists in plan.name, which this app itself always sets to
            "Every {N} days" when it creates the plan (see sellingPlanInput in
            app/models/sellingPlan.server.ts), so it's safe to parse back out.
            30+ days displays as whole months (30 -> "1 Month", 90 -> "3
            Months"); anything shorter stays as "Every N days" since it isn't
            evenly expressible in months.

            The bundle count comes from the plan's own second option value
            (options[1], the "Count" dimension the merchant fills in when
            saving plans in the app's admin) -- falls back to the day count
            for any plan saved before that field existed.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign name_parts = plan.name | split: " " -%}
          {%- assign day_count = name_parts[1] | plus: 0 -%}
          {%- if day_count >= 30 -%}
            {%- assign bundle_months = day_count | divided_by: 30 -%}
            {%- capture bundle_title -%}{{ bundle_months }} Month{% if bundle_months != 1 %}s{% endif %}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign bundle_title = plan.name | remove_first: "Every " -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- assign bundle_count = plan.options[1].value | default: day_count -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            options[2] is "Quantity" -- the real cart quantity added when
            this plan is selected (subscription-widget.js reads it via
            data-quantity), separate from bundle_count above which is just
            a display number. Falls back to 1 for plans saved before this
            existed.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign bundle_quantity = plan.options[2].value | default: 1 -%}

          <label class="subscription-widget__bundle-card" data-bundle-card>
            <input
              type="radio"
              name="subscription-widget-plan-{{ block.id }}"
              value="{{ plan.id }}"
              class="subscription-widget__bundle-radio-input"
              data-plan-radio
              data-days="{{ day_count }}"
              data-count="{{ bundle_count }}"
              data-quantity="{{ bundle_quantity }}"
              {% if forloop.first %}checked{% endif %}
            >
            {%- comment -%}
              The checkmark badge lives outside .bundle-body so the de-
              emphasis opacity applied to unselected cards (below) never
              dims it -- it needs to read as solid black the instant a card
              is checked, not a washed-out grey.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="subscription-widget__bundle-check" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="subscription-widget__bundle-body">
              <span class="subscription-widget__bundle-media">
                {%- if bundle_image -%}
                  <span class="subscription-widget__bundle-image">
                    {{ bundle_image | image_url: width: 160 | image_tag: loading: "lazy", alt: plan.name, widths: "80,160" }}
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="subscription-widget__bundle-badge" data-bundle-best-badge hidden>{{ block.settings.best_value_badge_text }}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="subscription-widget__bundle-text">
                <span class="subscription-widget__bundle-title">{{ bundle_title }}</span>
                {%- comment -%}
                  The count itself is static (Liquid-rendered from the plan's
                  own options), but the "$X / day" figure depends on live
                  price/selling-plan-discount data the same way every other
                  price in this widget does -- computed and filled in by
                  subscription-widget.js's render(), not hardcoded here.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <span class="subscription-widget__bundle-count">{{ bundle_count }} Count · <span data-bundle-per-day></span></span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </label>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

    </div>

    {%- if product.has_only_default_variant == false -%}
      {%- assign first_option = product.options_with_values.first -%}
      {%- assign new_values_list = block.settings.new_values | split: "," -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Merchants can name an exact flavor value in the block settings, but
        most won't bother -- so with nothing configured, default to the same
        pattern the design shows: the first flavor is "Most Favourite" and
        every other flavor is "New", rather than showing no badges at all.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign favourite_value = block.settings.favourite_value -%}
      {%- if favourite_value == blank -%}
        {%- assign favourite_value = first_option.values.first -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign new_values_configured = false -%}
      {%- if block.settings.new_values != blank -%}
        {%- assign new_values_configured = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Same "merchant types the exact flavor name" pattern as
        favourite_value/new_values above, but one line per flavor since each
        needs its own subtitle: "Flavor Name: subtitle text", one pair per
        line. Blank/unmatched flavors just show no subtitle.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign flavor_subtitle_lines = block.settings.flavor_subtitles | newline_to_br | split: "<br />" -%}

      <div class="subscription-widget__section">
        {%- if block.settings.flavor_step_label != blank -%}
          <p class="subscription-widget__step-label">{{ block.settings.flavor_step_label }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <p class="subscription-widget__flavor-heading">
          {{ block.settings.flavor_section_label }}
        </p>
        {%- comment -%}
          Multi-flavor mix picker: a plan with quantity > 1 lets the customer
          split that quantity across different flavors (e.g. 3 bottles = 2
          Sour Green Apple + 1 Blood Orange) instead of one flavor times the
          quantity. Tapping anywhere on a swatch adds one unit to it (the
          top-right "+" is just a visual cue, not a separate control) --
          there's no per-swatch count shown here; the "N/M selected" line
          and image-filled dot row below the grid is the only place the mix
          is reflected back. subscription-widget.js owns all the counting/
          redistribution logic and the total is capped at whatever quantity
          the selected plan allows -- these are just empty shells at render
          time.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="subscription-widget__swatch-grid">
          {%- for value in first_option.values -%}
            {%- assign swatch_variant = nil -%}
            {%- for v in product.variants -%}
              {%- if swatch_variant == nil and v.options[0] == value -%}
                {%- assign swatch_variant = v -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- assign swatch_image = swatch_variant.featured_image | default: product.featured_image -%}

            {%- assign is_favourite = false -%}
            {%- if value == favourite_value -%}
              {%- assign is_favourite = true -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign is_new = false -%}
            {%- if new_values_configured -%}
              {%- for new_value in new_values_list -%}
                {%- assign new_value_trimmed = new_value | strip -%}
                {%- if new_value_trimmed == value -%}
                  {%- assign is_new = true -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- elsif is_favourite == false -%}
              {%- assign is_new = true -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- assign flavor_subtitle = blank -%}
            {%- for line in flavor_subtitle_lines -%}
              {%- assign line_parts = line | split: ":" -%}
              {%- assign line_key = line_parts.first | strip -%}
              {%- if line_key == value -%}
                {%- assign flavor_subtitle = line | remove_first: line_key | remove_first: ":" | strip -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}

            <div
              class="subscription-widget__swatch"
              data-flavor-swatch
              data-variant-id="{{ swatch_variant.id }}"
              data-swatch-label="{{ value | escape }}"
            >
              {%- comment -%}
                The +/check button lives outside .swatch-body so the de-
                emphasis opacity applied to unselected swatches (below)
                never dims it -- it needs to read as solid black the
                instant a swatch is selected, not a washed-out grey.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <button type="button" class="subscription-widget__swatch-add-btn" data-qty-plus aria-label="Increase {{ value | escape }} quantity">+</button>
              <span class="subscription-widget__swatch-body">
                <span class="subscription-widget__swatch-image">
                  {%- if swatch_image -%}
                    {{ swatch_image | image_url: width: 160 | image_tag: loading: "lazy", alt: value, widths: "80,160" }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </span>
                <span class="subscription-widget__swatch-name">{{ value }}</span>
                {%- if flavor_subtitle != blank -%}
                  <span class="subscription-widget__swatch-subtitle">{{ flavor_subtitle }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if is_favourite and block.settings.favourite_badge_text != blank -%}
                  <span class="subscription-widget__swatch-badge subscription-widget__swatch-badge--favourite">{{ block.settings.favourite_badge_text }}</span>
                {%- elsif is_new and block.settings.new_badge_text != blank -%}
                  <span class="subscription-widget__swatch-badge subscription-widget__swatch-badge--new">{{ block.settings.new_badge_text }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        {%- comment -%}
          Progress readout: "N/M selected" plus one dot per unit the plan
          ships, filling in left-to-right as flavors are tapped. Always
          rendered, never hidden, so the placeholders show from page load.
          An unfilled dot stays a plain dashed placeholder; a filled one
          shows that unit's own flavor image with a small "x" to remove
          just that unit -- populated entirely by subscription-widget.js.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="subscription-widget__flavor-progress-label" data-flavor-remaining></p>
        <div class="subscription-widget__flavor-progress-dots" data-flavor-progress-dots aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </div>

      {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
        {%- if forloop.index0 > 0 -%}
          <div class="subscription-widget__section" data-option-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}">
            <p class="subscription-widget__section-label">{{ option.name }}</p>
            <div class="subscription-widget__option-values">
              {%- for value in option.values -%}
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="subscription-widget__option-value{% if value == current_variant.options[forloop.parentloop.index0] %} is-selected{% endif %}"
                  data-option-value="{{ value | escape }}"
                >
                  {{ value }}
                </button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Order summary card: mirrors whichever bundle card is currently
      selected above (title, discount, price, billing breakdown) -- all of
      it is computed live in subscription-widget.js off the same plan
      selection state the bundle grid uses, not hardcoded per plan.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="subscription-widget__order-summary">
      {%- for plan in selling_plan_group.selling_plans -%}
        {%- case forloop.index -%}
          {%- when 1 -%}{%- assign plan_badge_text = block.settings.order_summary_badge_text_1 -%}
          {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign plan_badge_text = block.settings.order_summary_badge_text_2 -%}
          {%- when 3 -%}{%- assign plan_badge_text = block.settings.order_summary_badge_text_3 -%}
          {%- else -%}{%- assign plan_badge_text = nil -%}
        {%- endcase -%}
        {%- if plan_badge_text != blank -%}
          <p class="subscription-widget__order-summary-banner" data-summary-banner-plan="{{ plan.id }}" {% unless forloop.first %}hidden{% endunless %}>{{ plan_badge_text }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      <div class="subscription-widget__order-summary-body">
        <div class="subscription-widget__order-summary-content">
          <div class="subscription-widget__order-summary-top">
            <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-title-group">
              <svg class="subscription-widget__order-summary-title-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8" stroke="#1E1E1E" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              </svg>
              <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-title" data-summary-title></span>
            </span>
            <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-save" data-summary-save></span>
          </div>
          <div class="subscription-widget__order-summary-price-row">
            <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-price" data-summary-price></span>
            <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-price-suffix">/ month</span>
            <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-compare" data-summary-compare></span>
          </div>
          <div class="subscription-widget__order-summary-billing">
            <span data-summary-billing></span>
            <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-per-serving" data-summary-per-serving></span>
          </div>

          {%- for plan in selling_plan_group.selling_plans -%}
            {%- case forloop.index -%}
              {%- when 1 -%}{%- assign plan_benefits = block.settings.order_summary_benefits_1 -%}
              {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign plan_benefits = block.settings.order_summary_benefits_2 -%}
              {%- when 3 -%}{%- assign plan_benefits = block.settings.order_summary_benefits_3 -%}
              {%- else -%}{%- assign plan_benefits = nil -%}
            {%- endcase -%}
            {%- if plan_benefits != blank -%}
              <div class="subscription-widget__order-summary-benefits" data-summary-benefits-plan="{{ plan.id }}" {% unless forloop.first %}hidden{% endunless %}>{{ plan_benefits }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-media">
          {%- if block.settings.order_summary_image -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              A merchant-picked photo (theme editor image_picker, same
              pattern as the bundle images above) -- static, so it doesn't
              change when the customer picks a different flavor.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {{ block.settings.order_summary_image | image_url: width: 300 | image_tag: loading: "lazy", alt: product.title, widths: "150,300" }}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              No photo configured -- fall back to mirroring whichever
              variant/flavor is currently selected, same image
              subscription-widget.js already resolves for the sticky bar
              (variant.featured_image, falling back to the product's own
              featured image). Hidden by default and only shown once
              render() finds an actual image, same pattern as the sticky
              bar's image.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <img data-summary-image alt="" loading="lazy" hidden>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Sits right below the bordered order-summary card, outside it --
      "Add to cart", the flavor-mix status message it reports on, and the
      one-time-purchase alternative are all deliberately NOT enclosed by the
      card's border.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="button" class="subscription-widget__order-summary-submit" data-add-to-cart-summary>
      {{ block.settings.order_summary_button_label }}
    </button>

    <p class="subscription-widget__status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

    <button type="button" class="subscription-widget__order-summary-onetime" data-add-to-cart-onetime>
      <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-onetime-label">One-time purchase</span> - <span data-summary-onetime-compare></span>
      <span data-summary-onetime-price></span>
      <span class="subscription-widget__order-summary-onetime-perday-wrap">(<span data-summary-onetime-perday></span> / Day)</span>
    </button>

    {%- comment -%}
      Hidden, not removed -- the order summary card above has its own "Add
      to cart" button wired to this exact same submit logic (see addToCart
      in subscription-widget.js), so this one's redundant now. It stays in
      the DOM because subscription-widget.js updates its text/disabled
      state unconditionally (no null-check) rather than being deleted and
      requiring a JS change to match.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="button" class="subscription-widget__submit" data-add-to-cart hidden>
      {{ block.settings.subscribe_button_label }}
    </button>
  </div>

  <script src="{{ 'subscription-widget.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'subscription-widget.css' | asset_url }}">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital@1&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%} Nothing to subscribe to -- stays empty so the theme's own buy box is what shows. Keeps a hook so the block is still selectable in the theme editor. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div data-subscription-widget-inactive {{ block.shopify_attributes }}></div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Subscription widget",
  "target": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Flavor / variant section" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "flavor_step_label", "label": "Flavor step eyebrow", "default": "Step 02 • Personalize Your Box", "info": "Small label above the heading. Leave blank to hide." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "flavor_section_label", "label": "Flavor section heading", "default": "Choose Your Flavors" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "swatch_selected_color", "label": "Selected flavor border / \"most favourite\" badge color", "default": "#1E1E1E" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "favourite_value", "label": "\"Most favourite\" flavor", "info": "Must exactly match one flavor value. Leave blank to hide." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "favourite_badge_text", "label": "Most-favourite badge text", "default": "Best Seller" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "new_values", "label": "\"New\" flavors", "info": "Comma-separated, must exactly match flavor values. Leave blank to hide." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "new_badge_text", "label": "New badge text", "default": "New" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "flavor_subtitles",
      "label": "Flavor subtitles",
      "info": "One per line, formatted as \"Flavor Name: subtitle text\" -- e.g. \"Sour Green Apple: Tart apple · Clean finish\". Leave a flavor out to show no subtitle for it.",
      "default": "Cherry Lime: Tart cherry · Lime finish\nSour Green Apple: Tart apple · Clean finish\nBlood Orange: Bold citrus · Smooth finish"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Plan section" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "plan_step_label", "label": "Plan step eyebrow", "default": "Step 01 • Build Your Ritual", "info": "Small label above the heading. Leave blank to hide." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "plan_section_label", "label": "Plan section heading", "default": "Choose Your Supply" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_best_value_badge", "label": "Show \"best value\" badge on the best-discount plan", "default": true },
